===A2_S4_D1===
// attached to oren or a chair at the waterfall place
Oren: Everyone, everyone, welcome! #portrait:Oren
Oren: With the Great Disaster’s return upon us, what better time to retell the tale of the last flood? #portrait:Oren
Oren: A tale of bravery and betrayal; of struggles and battles which changed the course of the world! #portrait:Oren
Oren: A tale that began with just two people, and a boat. #portrait:Oren 
// cutscene here
Oren: Once upon a time, a boy with a yearning heart was born in a distant land. // cutscene:A2S4_orenp1
Oren: His heart called for the great beyond — but his people shamed him for the foolish wish.
Oren: For they believed their home was blessed. A land without creatures nor storms. A haven which may only be touched by the Great Floods. 
Oren: His people could not spare a moment for his dreams. And so, as time grew, so did his restlessness. 
Oren: Until one day, he departed his homeland with his closest ally and friend. And maybe a little more? //cutscene:A2S4_orenp2
// cutscene here
Narrator: Oren winks, causing the crowd to huff out a laugh under their breaths. 
Oren: Together they sailed into the endless expanse. Mocked by their people and forbidden to return, they discovered joys and curiosities in the outside world. 
Oren: They discovered a world of creatures, and even landed on our Thavmian shores. Yes; they befriended many and learned from our vibrant, diverse strengths. Exchanging stories and skills.
// cutscene ends
Oren: But of course; there was an imminent issue… #portrait:Oren
Oren: The Great Disaster was due to come in a month. #portrait:Oren
Narrator: The main protagonist is Noah, an idealist who hoped to share the knowledge of wayfaring with others and connect them across the seas. #portrait:Oren
Narrator: While his best friend was Elio, a prodigy in sailing and building ships. A realist who’s loyal to those he holds dear.. #portrait:Oren
Narrator: After recounting more of the duo’s adventures, Oren wraps up the story on a cliffhanger; where Noah discovers that the Great Disaster was indeed a creature that could be found. 
Narrator: Not just a myth or turn of phrase. A real, breathing being, somewhere out in the seas.
Oren: Do return tomorrow evening for the conclusion of our brave duo’s tale! #portrait:Oren
Oren: I assure you, it’ll certainly be worth the wait. #portrait:Oren
Narrator: Oren smiles and chats with the lingering audience, soaking in the attention as if he’s done it all his life.
Chione: Hey, you two! How did you find the story? #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Narrator: Chione and Amaya appear from behind you. They must’ve been part of the standing crowd.
Amelia: The story about this Noah guy is pretty popular. Even I’ve heard it before. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: But… that stuff about his home island. Doesn’t it sound kind of familiar? #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Narrator: With all their eyes on you, you decide it’d be best not to lie, lest it gives them a reason to rescind their hospitality.
Noelle: Well… #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: You tell them about our island, and how you fled from it recently due to their stance on creatures.
Amaya: Dusk Island? #portrait:AmayaThink
Amaya: Can’t say I’ve heard of an island by that name. But due to the floods, many titles have also been changed and lost. #portrait:AmayaThink
Noelle: The Great Disaster… that’s what you guys call the creature behind the floods, right? #portrait:NoelleShocked
Amaya: Correct. #portrait:AmayaThink
Amaya: While Thavmia doesn’t get that many visitors, most people in the surrounding islands do call it by that name. #portrait:AmayaTalk
Noelle: Is Thavmia the name of this island? #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Chione: Yes! It’s named after the unique evolution of humans on our land. #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Narrator: Chione gestures to her own features and Amaya’s.
Chione: Due to how ancient Thavmia is, our human ancestors have since adapted to the regions they lived in over many generations. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Chione: We Viridi live in the forest, while other settlements go by different names. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Amaya: But aside from some biological evolution, we don’t have any special abilities. Not the kinds that Oren might make up for his stories, anyways. #portrait:AmayaThink
Noelle: I see… so there are other types of… uh. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Amaya: Thavma. #portrait:AmayaThink
Noelle: Thavma, on the island. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Amelia: Along with creatures, regular humans, and krakenfolk like you. #portrait:AmeliaHappy
Narrator: Amelia nudges your leg with an exasperated sigh.
Amelia: What <i>would</i> you have done if we hadn’t run into each other? #portrait:AmeliaShut
Narrator: Despite yourself, your lips quirk into a smile.
Noelle: I guess I would’ve lived on berries until the Great Floods came. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Chione: Well, you don’t have to do that now. #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Chione: But I wonder… could your homeland really be the same as Noah’s? #portrait:ChioneNormal
Noelle: There might be other places that are similar in geography… But the odd thing is, I‘ve never heard of this ‘Noah’ before. #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: (That is, unless he was written out of our history books.) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Chione: Is there anything else that’s different about your homeland? #portrait:ChioneHm
Narrator: Chione’s eyes have lit up excitedly.
Chione: What kind of animals live there? What is the climate like? #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Narrator: Chione’s sudden flurry of questions take you by surprise, but her excitement motivates you to grapple for a satisfying answer.
Noelle: Well, we only have regular humans there… Amelia’s actually the first creature I’ve met in my life. But I guess the climate is similar? Though ours is flatter and filled with more buildings than trees. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Amaya: Speaking of climate… I’ve handed the artifact and ore from earlier to Silas. He’s agreed that we can supply you with some wood in return for your work. #portrait:AmayaThink
Noelle: Really? Thank you so much! #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Amelia: Will we get to find out what the artifact’s about? #portrait:AmeliaHappy
Amaya: Hm… Probably, so long as it isn’t too sensitive. You did find it after all. #portrait:AmayaThink
Chione: We’ll probably have answers to that tomorrow! #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Amelia: Right… We’ve been running around all day. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Noelle: Tired already? #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Amelia: It’s hard with my size, you know! #portrait:AmeliaHostile
Amaya: Well, so long as you’re willing to adapt and listen to the world around you, there are other ways of surviving the floods. #portrait:AmayaThink
Chione: Right! We’ll tell you more about how Thavmia prepares tomorrow, if you’d like. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Amaya: Just go back and relax for now. #portrait:AmayaThink
// end of day 2 main story. Next step: sleep
-> DONE